    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161">

                <pb facs="0412" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg402"/>

                <head>S. Price Edwards, esq., collector of her Majesty’s customs, Liverpool, to
                    Laird Brothers.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Liverpool, September</hi> 11, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sirs:</hi> I am sorry to say there can be no
                    trial trip of the iron-clad ship until Earl Russell’s reply can be had. That
                    reply may yet come in time to meet your wishes.</p>
                <p>I am, dear sirs, yours, very truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. P. EDWARDS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laird Brothers.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
